\
Below is the version I would actually give Claude. It is deliberately written as an engineering specification rather than philosophical discussion.\
\
SageReasoning\
Cognitive OS + 12 Environment Architecture\
Engineering Handoff Specification\
1. Objective\
\
Extend the existing SageReasoning architecture into a stateful cognitive architecture consisting of:\
\
A shared Cognitive OS\
Twelve specialised cognitive environments\
Explicit epistemic state\
Belief revision and dependency tracking\
Temporal state/versioning\
Identity and narrative continuity\
Conversation and multi-agent interaction\
Structural coupling with environment/context\
Controlled inter-agent handoffs\
Immutable audit/trajectory history\
\
The purpose is not to simulate philosophical theories.\
\
The philosophical and cognitive theories are design sources from which we extract reliable computational primitives.\
\
The implementation must remain modular, deterministic wherever possible, inspectable, testable, and compatible with the existing SageReasoning Stoic harness.\
\
2. Architectural Principle\
\
The twelve environments are specialised reasoning environments.\
\
They are NOT twelve independent cognitive systems.\
\
They operate over shared Cognitive OS services.\
\
