9. Epistemic Debt Service\
\
Implement epistemic debt as a structured object, not merely a scalar.\
\
Track:\
\
unresolved claims\
unsupported assumptions\
contradictions\
unresolved counterarguments\
stale evidence\
missing information\
pending belief revisions\
\
Calculate:\
\
epistemic_debt_score\
\
as a derived summary.\
\
The score must never be treated as an objective measurement of truth.\
\
It is a system-management metric.\
\
Primary consumers:\
\
Laboratory\
Cellar\
Cloister\
Threshold\
Archive\
\
Threshold should be able to ask:\
\
What unresolved epistemic debt affects this decision?\
10. Identity / Narrative Service\
\
Create a first-class Identity State.\
\
The purpose is longitudinal continuity.\
\
Represent:\
\
values\
commitments\
stable preferences\
principles\
past commitments\
self-description\
narrative themes\
known tensions\
identity changes\
\
Example:\
\
\{\
  "identity_state_id": "uuid",\
  "version": 8,\
\
  "principles": [],\
  "commitments": [],\
  "values": [],\
\
  "narrative": \{\
    "themes": [],\
    "current_interpretation": ""\
  \},\
\
  "known_tensions": [],\
\
  "historical_commitments": [],\
\
  "timestamp": "ISO8601"\
\}\
\
Identity must remain distinguishable from epistemic truth.\
\
A claim is not true because it fits identity.\
\
Identity coherence answers:\
\
Does this belief, decision or action fit the currently maintained identity/commitment structure?\
\
It does not answer:\
\
Is the belief true?\
\
11. Identity Coherence\
\
Implement:\
\
identity_coherence_score\
\
as a derived alignment metric.\
\
Use it for:\
\
decision alignment\
commitment consistency\
longitudinal continuity\
detecting unexplained identity shifts\
\
Do NOT use it as a truth score.\
\
A system must be allowed to conclude:\
\
"This evidence contradicts my previous position."\
\
even when the new position reduces identity coherence.\
\
Such events should instead trigger reflection/revision.\
\
Primary owner:\
\
Cloister\
\
Secondary consumers:\
\
Threshold\
Archive\
