16. Handoff Protocol\
\
Every environment-to-environment handoff must use a standard envelope.\
\
Minimum:\
\
\{\
  "handoff_id": "uuid",\
\
  "from": "Laboratory",\
  "to": "Workshop",\
\
  "timestamp": "ISO8601",\
\
  "state": \{\
    "belief_state_id": "uuid",\
    "belief_state_version": 12\
  \},\
\
  "claims": [],\
\
  "epistemic_debt": \{\
    "score": 0.23,\
    "relevant_items": []\
  \},\
\
  "identity": \{\
    "state_id": "uuid",\
    "version": 4,\
    "coherence_score": 0.87\
  \},\
\
  "events": [],\
\
  "payload": \{\}\
\}\
\
Additional fields should be included only when relevant.\
\
Do NOT require a DEL event on every handoff.\
\
Require an event reference whenever the handoff represents a meaningful state transition.\
\
17. Read/Write Discipline\
\
This is a hard architectural constraint.\
\
Every Cognitive OS service must expose explicit permissions:\
\
READ\
CREATE\
UPDATE\
REVISE\
RETRACT\
COMMIT\
\
Environments must not have unrestricted access to shared state.\
\
For example:\
\
Forest:\
READ claims\
CREATE hypotheses\
NO direct COMMIT\
\
Laboratory:\
READ evidence\
CREATE/REVISE claims\
NO identity modification\
\
Cloister:\
READ identity\
PROPOSE identity revision\
NO alteration of factual evidence\
\
Threshold:\
READ all decision-relevant state\
COMMIT decisions\
\
The permission model must be machine-enforced rather than merely documented.\
\
18. Stoic Harness Integration\
\
The existing deterministic Stoic harness remains a separate philosophical/decision layer.\
\
It receives:\
\
current belief state\
relevant claims\
epistemic debt\
identity/commitment state\
decision context\
constraints\
proposed action\
\
The Stoic harness should evaluate the proposed action against the existing Stoic framework.\
\
It must NOT become responsible for managing the Cognitive OS.\
\
Conceptually:\
\
Cognitive OS\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Current epistemic + identity state\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Threshold\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Stoic Harness\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Decision evaluation\
      \uc0\u8595 \
Commit / reject / revise\
\
The Stoic layer is therefore a decision-integrity mechanism operating on state, not the state-management mechanism itself.\
\
