\
Final decisions should use a durable record.\
\
\{\
  "decision_id": "uuid",\
\
  "action": "string",\
\
  "belief_state_id": "uuid",\
  "belief_state_version": 15,\
\
  "supporting_claims": [],\
\
  "known_uncertainties": [],\
\
  "epistemic_debt_score": 0.18,\
\
  "identity_state_id": "uuid",\
  "identity_coherence_score": 0.91,\
\
  "adversarial_test_results": [],\
\
  "stoic_evaluation": \{\},\
\
  "provenance": [],\
\
  "commitment_event_id": "uuid",\
\
  "timestamp": "ISO8601"\
\}\
\
Decisions must be immutable after commitment.\
\
A later change produces a new event/version rather than mutating history.\
\
20. Reopening Decisions\
\
A committed decision must be reopenable.\
\
Trigger examples:\
\
critical evidence invalidated\
supporting claim retracted\
major assumption challenged\
environment changed materially\
identity commitment changed materially\
new contradictory evidence\
constraint violation\
\
Flow:\
\
New evidence\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Laboratory\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Belief Revision\
     \uc0\u8595 \
TMS dependency propagation\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Affected decisions identified\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Threshold notified\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Cloister / Cellar / Arena as appropriate\
     \uc0\u8595 \
Decision reopened\
\
This is a core capability.\
\
21. Epistemic Debt + Decision Gate\
\
Before Threshold commits a consequential decision, run:\
\
1. What claims support this decision?\
2. What assumptions support those claims?\
3. Which dependencies are uncertain?\
4. What unresolved counterarguments exist?\
5. What evidence is stale?\
6. What would cause the decision to be reopened?\
7. What identity/commitment tensions exist?\
8. What adversarial tests have been performed?\
\
The system should be able to produce:\
\
DECISION READY\
\
or:\
\
DECISION REQUIRES REVIEW\
\
with explicit reasons.\
\
Do not reduce this to a single threshold score.\
\
22. Environment Selection\
\
The autonomous agent layer should eventually select environments based on state and goal.\
\
Do not initially make this fully autonomous.\
\
First implement explicit routing.\
\
Example:\
\
Goal\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Library \uc0\u8594  Laboratory\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Forest\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Garden\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Cellar\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Arena\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Cloister\
 \uc0\u8595 \
Threshold\
\
But routing must be state-dependent.\
\
For example:\
\
If evidence weak:\
    Laboratory\
\
If assumptions unstable:\
    Cellar\
\
If old/rejected idea may be relevant:\
    Attic\
\
If conceptual alternatives required:\
    Forest\
\
If cross-domain integration required:\
    Garden\
\
If adversarial risk high:\
    Arena\
\
If identity/commitment tension exists:\
    Cloister\
\
Later the autonomous agent can learn/select these routes.\
\
